{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future","id":1446753,"title":"CoD: any plans for the future?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-01T00:38:20-07:00","id":1446753,"title":"CoD: any plans for the future?","content":"Is there anything new planned for the CoD from Onyx Path?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26374-shadowchaser","name":"Shadowchaser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:41:54-07:00","id":1446827,"title":"","content":"There are a few Kickstarter achieved products which are at work. If there is anything beside the products we already know about (most of which are already being at the MMN), we'll probably see them at the coming brochure for the next year","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:37:41-07:00","id":1447214,"title":"","content":"I am eager to see what game line they have planned to follow Deviant. I'm struggling to think of an idea for a game line that's both enticing enough to stand alone and not redundant with a line that already exists... although maybe that speaks more to my own lack of creativity than anything else. XD<br /> <br /> Maybe something like Alien? Whether your character comes from space, an alternate reality, another plane of existence (maybe one that already exists in CoD or one that's heretofore unheard of), or otherwise, you're playing as someone or something that's just not native to Earth as we know it. Goals could involve trying to assimilate yourself into humanity as best you can, trying to find a way to return to your home, or even taking over or bringing more of your own people here. Maybe not every Alien is somebody who was accidentally stranded, lost, or fled as a refugee, they could also come here as would-be conquerors or terraformers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","name":"RuNoMai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T11:15:57-07:00","id":1447421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RuNoMai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1447214#post1447214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am eager to see what game line they have planned to follow Deviant. I'm struggling to think of an idea for a game line that's both enticing enough to stand alone and not redundant with a line that already exists... although maybe that speaks more to my own lack of creativity than anything else. XD<br /> <br /> Maybe something like Alien? Whether your character comes from space, an alternate reality, another plane of existence (maybe one that already exists in CoD or one that's heretofore unheard of), or otherwise, you're playing as someone or something that's just not native to Earth as we know it. Goals could involve trying to assimilate yourself into humanity as best you can, trying to find a way to return to your home, or even taking over or bringing more of your own people here. Maybe not every Alien is somebody who was accidentally stranded, lost, or fled as a refugee, they could also come here as would-be conquerors or terraformers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait for the Clade Companion when it comes out before pitching Alien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T10:07:14-07:00","id":1447595,"title":"","content":"if we're talking hopeful future plans. <br /> <br /> I'm far more interested in companion/supplement books for the second edition lines rather then whole new game lines. <br /> I don't know the metrics on how well supplemental books sell, but i have full collections for Promethean, Changeling, Hunter, Geist Demon, and Mummy. (even though the last three especially Geist are a little light on published material.)<br /> Way back i used to think that each line (other the the big three) would get four supplements and to me that seemed perfect. <br /> <br /> Second edition is obviously tricky because many people don't want to buy books that are basically doubles of books they own, so you can't retread the old ground step for step. but at the same time wild deviations can also devalue the usefulness of first edition books or just alienate fans.<br /> I have always treated the NWoD as a tool box and believe the second edition needs to lean into that more then it has been. In my mind second edition should be updates and variations rather then reprints and overwrites.<br /> <br /> This is all just my musings though. I've supported the NWoD for ten plus years and I'm looking forward to them pulling out of this slump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T20:11:07-07:00","id":1447689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1447595#post1447595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second edition is obviously tricky because many people don't want to buy books that are basically doubles of books they own, so you can't retread the old ground step for step. but at the same time wild deviations can also devalue the usefulness of first edition books or just alienate fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>The good news is that OPP seems to be on the same line of thinking as you.<br /> <br /> They said that for CofD 2e, they try to avoid as much as they can going the route of &quot;convert 1e thing to 2e thing&quot; with books. Granted, for stuff like a particular 1e Bloodline that doesn't have an official 2e write up, that means you're the one stuck with trying to convert it over.<br /> <br /> Either way, at least good to know that for future books they try to focus on new Stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T04:15:43-07:00","id":1447706,"title":"","content":"I just want werewolf and vampire and mage and all the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T12:15:24-07:00","id":1447963,"title":"","content":"As a Storyteller, the Night Horrors books have all been great, I would love to see more of them.<br /> <br /> I hope that Werewolf gets some more love. Forsaken changed more between 1e and 2e than either Requiem or Awakening in my opinion, so porting over 1e material is much more difficult. The situation with Lodges is particularly bad, right now there are only 4 playable 2e Lodges (Temple of Apollo is not going to be appropriate in most games, and even Eaters of the Dead are stretching acceptability quite a bit). I'm not saying that I want all the 1e Lodges updated, but it feels like the Tribal Pillars at least should get that treatment, and I would love to see more brand new 2e Lodges. There are a few other mechanical gaps in Forsaken 2e - alternate Moon gifts are hinted at, but we only have 1 example so far from the blog, and it would be nice to get more Wolf Gifts since these are a new concept with 2e, but so far we only have 3 examples (plus a fourth from the blog).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T14:24:35-07:00","id":1447986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1447963#post1447963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Storyteller, the Night Horrors books have all been great, I would love to see more of them.<br /> <br /> I hope that Werewolf gets some more love. Forsaken changed more between 1e and 2e than either Requiem or Awakening in my opinion, so porting over 1e material is much more difficult. The situation with Lodges is particularly bad, right now there are only 4 playable 2e Lodges (Temple of Apollo is not going to be appropriate in most games, and even Eaters of the Dead are stretching acceptability quite a bit). I'm not saying that I want all the 1e Lodges updated, but it feels like the Tribal Pillars at least should get that treatment, and I would love to see more brand new 2e Lodges. There are a few other mechanical gaps in Forsaken 2e - alternate Moon gifts are hinted at, but we only have 1 example so far from the blog, and it would be nice to get more Wolf Gifts since these are a new concept with 2e, but so far we only have 3 examples (plus a fourth from the blog).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same feeling. I've had quite a few WtF1st chronicles and I'm thrilled by the changes in the 2nd but I feel I risk porting in a bad way the knowledge and experience I have gained in these years. I'd like more on spirits and the hisil, instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26374-shadowchaser","name":"Shadowchaser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T16:02:14-07:00","id":1448079,"title":"","content":"I'd love a Night Horrors book aimed at the core line's &quot;mostly regular people investigating the supernatural&quot; theme. Fill it with gruesome ghosts, goblins, and ghouls who don't fit into the social monster books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T02:33:17-07:00","id":1448110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448079#post1448079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love a Night Horrors book aimed at the core line's &quot;mostly regular people investigating the supernatural&quot; theme. Fill it with gruesome ghosts, goblins, and ghouls who don't fit into the social monster books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be cool. Maybe we'll get something like that for Hunter 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T13:11:54-07:00","id":1448530,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Night Horrors books, I really hope that we get one for <i>Changeling: The Lost </i>2E. I really enjoyed the Night Horrors book for first edition <i>Changeling.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T07:22:12-07:00","id":1448775,"title":"","content":"Future plans didn't come up in the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-Vhw3tkDKM&amp;t\" target=\"_blank\">What's Up With Onyx Path table</a> beyond the stuff we already know, Deviant and Mummy are almost out, Hunter's next, they've got some supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T15:50:46-07:00","id":1448812,"title":"","content":"That sounds disappointing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T22:57:53-07:00","id":1448941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448812#post1448812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds disappointing...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. They've explained two things that happen to cause it. One, they don't seem able to put things on the list until it's been given an okay by Paradox. And two, they're putting a lot of effort into finishing the Kickstarter fulfillments. It's understandable, Mummy, Deviant, Hunter, all are cores which require a lot of work.<br /> <br /> But the Paradox thing is a big mystery. Like we don't know if Paradox is saying no to everything, or if nothing's being pitched for Chronicles. Or both.<br /> <br /> Still, 'dropping the line' seems a far fetched fear. It's profits, they know the line. If Paradox was refusing everything, then they'd have no reason to keep up the license, as well. And if either were happening they'd probably make an announcement about it.<br /> <br /> So it seems like stuff is just going slow while they focus on the big books coming out. And they may make some announcements during the upcoming Con. Ideally (for us) they'll be Chronicles stuff. Could certainly use more Werewolf the Forsaken content and I'm sure fans of other games want more of theirs.<br /> <br /> From this Monday Meeting blog post, 'I do know that we\u2019ll be having the latest in the \u201cWhat\u2019s Up With Onyx Path?\u201d panels, and for those of you who love announcements, you\u2019ll be thrilled to know that we\u2019ll be <b>announcing some awesome new projects</b> at the panel!' And it was already in bold. Plus they're getting a brochure out. While the Chronicles sections of the brochure seem to shrink every time we see them in favor of all the new games (and old games) maybe we'll get some new stuff. Can only hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-19-2021, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T01:04:43-07:00","id":1448950,"title":"","content":"I think that Paradox just silently kills <b>CoD</b> lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They make all the 2E corebooks cause there where corebooks announced before acquisition - made Kickstarters after it, and so the fans cannot complain 'you just dropped our game by acquisition'. They end all 2E corebooks and that will be all. The <b>WoD</b> line is ruling in all the way and <u>we should not look for the new supplements for <b>CoD</b></u>. It's typical corporation practice - buy your own biggest competition (<b> WoD </b>vs <b>CoD </b>) and slowly kill the previous completion, making 'reforms' and 'reconstructions' that 'by mistake' 'not works'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Making <b>CoD</b> line is costly - from <b>Paradox</b> perspective, why to put money in it, when 5E <b>WoD </b>sells well?<br /> <br /> I already move to <b>Scion</b> and <b>Storypath</b>, as without supplements, <b>CoD</b> 2E has too much holes in it to run it easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-19-2021, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T01:13:50-07:00","id":1448951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448950#post1448950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Paradox just silently kills <b>CoD</b> lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no decisive, tangible proof to suggest that this is true at all. Frankly the sentiment with the &quot;What's Up with Onyx Path?&quot; panel is just consistent with what we've been told before then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T01:36:08-07:00","id":1448952,"title":"","content":"It just my feels. I change my assumptions if any new <b>CoD</b> product will be announced, outside of Kickstarters fulfilment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T04:44:45-07:00","id":1448964,"title":"","content":"Does Paradox have any say at all in what CoD material gets made? I thought OPP had leased the intellectual property?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T05:00:00-07:00","id":1448966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448964#post1448964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Paradox have any say at all in what CoD material gets made? I thought OPP had leased the intellectual property?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. They can pitch products to be made and can veto any propositions tossed to by freelancers. It's their property, and as such all such things have to be approved by them.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, I don't really think Paradox particularly gets in the way or delays Chronicles-and I say this as someone who has no love lost for Paradox. They don't particularly care about it, but the attitude they've always displayed is that they see it has a fanbase and that Onyx Path knows how to curate that fanbase. Nothing about the way Chronicles has been developed has actually changed all that much in the last decade.<br /> <br /> They don't commission stuff regularly like they do for World, which doesn't hurt or help any more than anything CCP did. Honestly, I think the answer given, that there's a lot of attention at the moment to catching up on projects they already started, is the the actual case-it IS s long laundry list.<br /> <br /> It's easy to think of Paradox as the villain here, but sometimes the most banal reasoning is the most accurate answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-19-2021, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T11:06:59-07:00","id":1449013,"title":"","content":"Considering that new gamelines were opened for the STV not that long ago (Geist, Deviant and the Contagion, IIRC), I do not think that we can say that Paradox kills CofD- if they did, they wouldn't support it in such manner, I think. As it stands, we don't even know if it is Paradox who does not approve pitches or Onyx Path who does not pitch. At least with the STV being open freelancers and devs may add supplements through this medium if they are interested in it, but I do hope that CofD will get more attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T20:05:45-07:00","id":1449080,"title":"","content":"I think writers or developers pitch to Rich, who decides if it's worth catching. Then Rich either tosses it up to Paradox, or has a more fleshed out pitch set up and tosses it up then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T10:06:16-07:00","id":1449128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1449080#post1449080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think writers or developers pitch to Rich, who decides if it's worth catching. Then Rich either tosses it up to Paradox, or has a more fleshed out pitch set up and tosses it up then.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T12:40:28-07:00","id":1449132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no decisive, tangible proof to suggest that this is true at all. Frankly the sentiment with the &quot;What's Up with Onyx Path?&quot; panel is just consistent with what we've been told before then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I share Hamster's sentiment. Of course there would be no tangible proof, there are still products being released, if there's a formal announcement it'd be a heavy hit on the sales of products yet to be released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T12:54:44-07:00","id":1449133,"title":"","content":"Well if they are secretly killing it, they're doing a bad job of it. Two of the more recent new books announced were Changeling's the Hedge and Mage's Tome of the Pentacle, neither of which were part of a Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T13:01:23-07:00","id":1449134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1449133#post1449133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if they are secretly killing it, they're doing a bad job of it. Two of the more recent new books announced were Changeling's the Hedge and Mage's Tome of the Pentacle, neither of which were part of a Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tome of pentacle had alread been approved a long time ago - a year or 2 ago iirc -. Mage also has another book which has been previously approved, &quot;fallen worlds&quot; (or something like that).<br /> <br /> I'm not so up-to-date with Changeling stuff but iirc the Hedge is also a book that had been approved back in 2019. Btw, 2019 seems to be the shifting point, cuz all we have ongoing right now or yet to be released had already been announced back then. 2 years and no genuinely new announcements... that is worrying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T13:25:22-07:00","id":1449136,"title":"","content":"If Paradox cancelled the setting they likely wouldn't care about games that were announced years ago, and Onyx Path could save time and money not holding onto the license, hiring artists and writers for them to keep up some charade and just focusing on other things.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that it doesn't seem like Chronicles is getting as many books as I'd like, but there being a secret cancelling that still allows Kickstarters and new games and new books but doesn't allow all new books, but might because they were announced years ago by both companies which would probably be better off just announcing it and moving on is getting a little fantastical. Especially considering the extra factor of Exalted, which Paradox hasn't expressed any interest in, is a licensed property, and is also making previously unannounced projects, or making new announcements for projects.<br /> <br /> More likely it's just a perception thing. Right now there's 14 Chronicles books at various stages of open development, including 3 core books (which are the more cost and people intensive books to make). There's 12 lines, more if you include Dark Eras and Contagion, and no supplement treadmill and a focus on trying to get the Kickstarter rewards fulfilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Toned down 05-20-2021, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T13:30:03-07:00","id":1449138,"title":"","content":"And there is a precedent of PDX canceling books after said books had already been announced by OPP.<br /> <br /> In particular, W20 Tribebook: Bunyip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T01:21:36-07:00","id":1451812,"title":"","content":"So... I'm out of town and will be until sunday night. Has there been any mention of new stuff for any cofd line? I just downloaded the brochure aaaand... Nothing there that we haven't been aware of for the past couple of years.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow there will be a cofd panel, right? If anyone here watches it, can you post if they talk about anything new?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T01:31:29-07:00","id":1451816,"title":"","content":"The brochure doesn't have new or just announced stuff stuff. There were a few new things mentioned in the opening ceremonies that weren't on the brochure. Aether, for Trinity, which seems to be War of the Worlds and Victorian Steampunk maybe with a little Princes of Amber. And Pugmire has some Underworld thing coming that will introduce psionics (and burrowing animals, I guess).<br /> <br /> It doesn't look good. I asked repeatedly if there was going to be any announcements for the line. A yes or no question. But was just told what we've all been told before 'Paradox needs to okay.' The same thing that happened during one of the podcast 'Ask us anything' and the same thing that happened at one of the last virtual cons. The inability to just get a straight answer is irritating and suggests a no, especially when other announcements were being made.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles one will be on Sunday (1 PM, EST, so in about 32 hours from this post). And yes, I'll mention any new announcements (unless someone else does it first).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2021, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T01:43:39-07:00","id":1451817,"title":"","content":"As far as I know there are only two cofd books that aren't in any stage of the monday blog notes which are for mtaw: fallen worlds and another one that Dave has mentioned before he left his dev post but hasn't been named yet. Both were, allegedly, already approved.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I'm getting more and more unsure if even these will fly. And afaik, no other cofd line has yet-to-enter-monday-posts books, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T05:10:32-07:00","id":1451831,"title":"","content":"I will just reiterate myself... ( read full original post for details ) I want to be proven wrong by OPP...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448950#post1448950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Paradox just silently kills <b>CoD</b> lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (...)<br /> I already move to <b>Scion</b> and <b>Storypath</b>, as without supplements, <b>CoD</b> 2E has too much holes in it to run it easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only add to that <b>T</b><b>hey Came From</b> gamelines from<b> Storypath</b> have various of genres in them - and <b>Beyond the Grave </b>and <b>Camp Murder Lake</b> is basically <b>CoD</b>-lite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2021, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:05:14-07:00","id":1451840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1451816#post1451816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The brochure doesn't have new or just announced stuff stuff. There were a few new things mentioned in the opening ceremonies that weren't on the brochure. Aether, for Trinity, which seems to be War of the Worlds and Victorian Steampunk maybe with a little Princes of Amber. And Pugmire has some Underworld thing coming that will introduce psionics (and burrowing animals, I guess).</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the fact that Demon, Promethean, and Werewolf weren't even mentioned in the brochure to be extremely concerning. Are those lines just cancelled now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1451816#post1451816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't look good. I asked repeatedly if there was going to be any announcements for the line. A yes or no question. But was just told what we've all been told before 'Paradox needs to okay.' The same thing that happened during one of the podcast 'Ask us anything' and the same thing that happened at one of the last virtual cons. The inability to just get a straight answer is irritating and suggests a no, especially when other announcements were being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me like this just confirms what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> has been saying. Either OPP aren't asking, or Paradox aren't saying yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T08:58:53-07:00","id":1451864,"title":"","content":"We've got this con to see. Like I said, outlook not so good, but there's two panels they might make announcements. The 'Whats up with Onyx Path?' one today at 1 EST or the Chronicles of Darkness one, same time tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Looks like I was wrong about the What's up panel, it was at noon. Seems like they just talked about Exalted, Pugmire and Scion. Exalted is also a Paradox owned property but no mention of them having to ask Paradox for anything related to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2021, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T09:43:07-07:00","id":1451869,"title":"","content":"While one might argue that some lines have enough 2e books as is, say... Demon, Vampire and maybe even Beast, other lines are pretty supplement starved such as Promethean and Geist.<br /> <br /> Damn, Geist has so many things that can be covered in 2e, in particular because 1e Geist was also book starved. At the very, very least it deserves a Night Horrors of its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:13:39-07:00","id":1452018,"title":"","content":"Okay. The line isn't dead. But they're not allowed to talk about possibilities. Most of the Chronicles of Darkness talk was focused on books already announced, Kith &amp; Kin, the Hedge, Deviant Companion, Contagion Player's Guide and a little on Tome of Pentacle. Questions about other lines, you'll basically have to bug Paradox about it. Though they didn't give any address and it seems given the Leviathan DLC they'll only really respond if you tank reviews en masse. They did say there had been no pitches for a 12th line, and the (the four panelists) had no ideas for one, except Eric Zawadzki who seemed to like the idea of a new Mirrors.<br /> <br /> The gist is that the line doesn't seem dead but Paradox does seem to be tightening the screws, if they're unable to even talk about potential future stuff. I have no idea how we'd ask Paradox anything about this. Apparently people at Paradox really liked Damnation City, which might be one of the reasons Justin Achilli was tasked with doing Vampire the Masquerade for Paradox, along with his past on the line. It's disheartening to not know anything about the health of the lines, and it's exacerbated by being told that we'd have to ask an entirely other company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-13-2021, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:21:00-07:00","id":1452021,"title":"","content":"We could try to just email paradox. Giving then some feedback,asking them to let Onyx Path do more books.<br /> We'd have to be polite about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:34:41-07:00","id":1452025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452021#post1452021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could try to just email paradox. Giving then some feedback,asking them to let Onyx Path do more books.<br /> We'd have to be polite about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to know <i>how</i> to go about contacting them. I looked before, but wasn't able to find an email on either <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/</a> or <a href=\"https://www.paradoxplaza.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxplaza.com/</a><br /> <br /> I've been willing to forgive Paradox for quite a lot in the past with their video games, but killing CofD is enough to completely put me off them as a company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:43:06-07:00","id":1452027,"title":"","content":"A few days ago Ian Watson has told me over twitter that the same crew responsible for WoD IS the crew responsible for CofD. <br /> Let's organize ourselves in a discord server of our own and coordinate efforts on asking these WoD folks wtf is going on with their management of CofD lines.<br /> I won't be home until tomorrow, but feel free to create a server and shoot me an invite via inbox.<br /> <br /> Or find me on opp's official server, I go by the same name there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:59:22-07:00","id":1452029,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I interpreted the discussion as all that doom &amp; gloomy. They have a pretty large backlog of books in the works as it stands, it seems reasonable they'd be fully occupied at the moment. <br /> <br /> I could see wanting to get at least Hunter, Mummy, and Deviant out the door before announcing the future books that might be a long time away or consumed by the usual churn of production problems. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T12:12:27-07:00","id":1452031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452027#post1452027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's organize ourselves in a discord server of our own and coordinate efforts on asking these WoD folks wtf is going on with their management of CofD lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in joining the Discord on that subject to help - but not to lead it. As I written before - I'm a bit heartbroken already over <b>CoD</b> and moved my games to <b>Scion</b>.<br /> <br /> BTW, there is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1423866-scion-mage-the-awakening\"><b>Scion </b>topic how to recreate <b>CoD</b> splats in it</a>, if you are interested...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T12:49:38-07:00","id":1452036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452031#post1452031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested in joining the Discord on that subject to help - but not to lead it. As I written before - I'm a bit heartbroken already over <b>CoD</b> and moved my games to <b>Scion</b>.<br /> <br /> BTW, there is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1423866-scion-mage-the-awakening\"><b>Scion </b>topic how to recreate <b>CoD</b> splats in it</a>, if you are interested...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I guess I'm not all that invested these days either. As much as I like the game writing, I find the game design of the CofD to be inelegant, irritatingly fiddly, and dated (or at least out of step with my taste in games these days). So I mostly pick up the books out of nostalgia, boredom, and to steal ideas for Urban Shadows or Monster of the Week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 06-13-2021, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:54:59-07:00","id":1452073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452029#post1452029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see wanting to get at least Hunter, Mummy, and Deviant out the door before announcing the future books that might be a long time away or consumed by the usual churn of production problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been my stance as well. I'm not going to be super concerned about the future of CofD until after the remaining 2e corebooks and the Stretch Goal books are all out.<br /> <br /> Plus, the impression I get is that the Brochures and Cons are no longer reliable when it comes to announcements. That considering past-announced books include a bevy of books that haven't appeared in the MMN (WtF's Secrets of the Tribes, Innocents 2e, etc), and per OPP's usual policy of &quot;no announcing release dates of books until week(s) away from release&quot;, I imagine that's a tactic they want to shy away from so as not to get fans frustrated at announcing a book's existence but then hearing nothing about it for years and years.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T08:23:42-07:00","id":1452165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452073#post1452073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has been my stance as well. I'm not going to be super concerned about the future of CofD until after the remaining 2e corebooks and the Stretch Goal books are all out.</div> </div> </div> </div>By then it might be too late, what if pdx is just waiting for the current books to go through the pipeline to formally shut it down at the end? This is corporate 101.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:46:03-07:00","id":1452223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452165#post1452165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By then it might be too late, what if pdx is just waiting for the current books to go through the pipeline to formally shut it down at the end? This is corporate 101.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a point where healthy concern descends into doomcrying and this is getting well past the line.<br /> <br /> It's been a rough couple years for the world and RPGs in general have been slow for years. Chill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T03:18:29-07:00","id":1458799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1451869#post1451869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While one might argue that some lines have enough 2e books as is, say... Demon, Vampire and maybe even Beast, other lines are pretty supplement starved such as Promethean and Geist.<br /> <br /> Damn, Geist has so many things that can be covered in 2e, in particular because 1e Geist was also book starved. At the very, very least it deserves a Night Horrors of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that even <b>Werewolf</b> 2E do not have proper support for 2 of 5 their main Tribes antagonists, even now, with <b>Shunned by the Moon</b> - namely. Spirit-Ridden/Claimed and Hosts do not have proper mechanics in 2E to run them as antagonists for Hunters in Darkness and Storm Lords - you just got bunch of random examples for them, not detailing any more concrete, like powers or banishing/fighting tactics. At least Pure got their new powers...<br /> <br /> But talk over it I may move to <b>WtF</b> forum on that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T04:09:09-07:00","id":1458805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1458799#post1458799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that even <b>Werewolf</b> 2E do not have proper support for 2 of 5 their main Tribes antagonists, even now, with <b>Shunned by the Moon</b> - namely. Spirit-Ridden/Claimed and Hosts do not have proper mechanics in 2E to run them as antagonists for Hunters in Darkness and Storm Lords - you just got bunch of random examples for them, not detailing any more concrete, like powers or banishing/fighting tactics. At least Pure got their new powers...<br /> <br /> But talk over it I may move to <b>WtF</b> forum on that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is a particularly bad example of something a lot of CofD books are guilty of: hiding important rules inside of conditions and powers. As an example, the rules for standing up in combat are hidden in the resolution mechanic for the knocked down tilt, rather than in the combat section, and not all of the core books reprint this particular tilt (looking at you Vampire).<br /> <br /> The rules for Spirit Ridden are the same way. The Claimed manifestation on page 191 of Werewolf explains what happens mechanically when a Spirit claims a person or object and how it can end. Spirit Ridden can also be just possessed or controlled, which are again explained under those manifestations. I believe you are supposed to extrapolate that those rules in chapter 4 explain how the entities in chapter 5 were built, but the game never tells you that.<br /> <br /> Hosts on the other hand are worse. As best I can tell, the examples we have were built using the Horrors rules from the CofD core (which aren't reprinted in Werewolf) and given thematically/species appropriate Dread Power from page 210/211 of Werewolf. It's easy to miss, but the section on page 203 just before Funnel-Web explains which Dread Powers the Shartha tend to develop based on their species and the stage in their lifecycle. One essential rule that was missing was the mechanics for a Host invading a Human's body. This appears along with a treatment of how large their essence pools should be on page 107 of Shunned by the Moon. <hr /><br /> Getting back to the topic at hand, I'm pretty concerned that we're approaching the one year mark since a new CofD product entered the Monday meeting Notes (last was The Hedge 10 months ago) and the two year mark since we got a new Kickstarter (the last was Hunter 2e 18 months ago). I'm not sure at what point it becomes fair to say that the line has been abandoned, but those seem like two valid milestones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","user":"Aurumae","date":". 09-05-2021, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T07:48:58-07:00","id":1458831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1458805#post1458805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the topic at hand, I'm pretty concerned that we're approaching the one year mark since a new CofD product entered the Monday meeting Notes (last was The Hedge 10 months ago) and the two year mark since we got a new Kickstarter (the last was Hunter 2e 18 months ago). I'm not sure at what point it becomes fair to say that the line has been abandoned, but those seem like two valid milestones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said this less than three months ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1452223#post1452223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a point where healthy concern descends into doomcrying and this is getting well past the line.<br /> <br /> It's been a rough couple years for the world and RPGs in general have been slow for years. Chill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eighty-three days is not enough time to change my stance on this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T10:41:46-07:00","id":1458849,"title":"","content":"If I'm getting pinged over to this thread <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2384_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2384\" data-vbnamecard=\"2384\">Aurumae</a> my stance hasn't changed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\"> CoD: any plans for the future? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Is there anything new planned for the CoD from Onyx Path? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T23:08:21-07:00","id":1458951,"title":"","content":"Chronicles is being killed?<br /> <br /> *looks at contracts*<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T05:12:25-07:00","id":1458992,"title":"","content":"will we get a subforum for <i>Deviant ?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T07:50:52-07:00","id":1459008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1458992#post1458992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">will we get a subforum for <i>Deviant ?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely. As I understand it, there are some tech issues with adding any additional subforums, and nobody currently within OPP has the skill sets needed to overcome them (at least not without potentially wiping years of existing threads).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T18:25:51-07:00","id":1459225,"title":"","content":"OnyxPath has been very generous in the past on announcing projects and giving previews. Honestly I think this is really to there detriment, I think this thread is an example of that. It possible that they are turning down the flow of information for their own benefit, which I think would be smart. If I was running OP, I wouldn't even mention a product until a first draft has been turned in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T04:17:21-07:00","id":1460016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1459225#post1459225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OnyxPath has been very generous in the past on announcing projects and giving previews. Honestly I think this is really to there detriment, I think this thread is an example of that. It possible that they are turning down the flow of information for their own benefit, which I think would be smart. If I was running OP, I wouldn't even mention a product until a first draft has been turned in.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you do that when a lot of the projects are Kickstarter funded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T04:47:22-07:00","id":1460017,"title":"","content":"I honestly just hope we will soon see some new books announced for Werewolf, Vampire and Mage.<br /> I know about dark eras, but I really feel those great lines are dying. I strongly think the big 3 need more books for their amazing lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T07:07:30-07:00","id":1460029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460017#post1460017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly just hope we will soon see some new books announced for Werewolf, Vampire and Mage.<br /> I know about dark eras, but I really feel those great lines are dying. I strongly think the big 3 need more books for their amazing lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>One problem, for Werewolf at least, is that that line was actually kind of <i>too</i> well developed over it's run. THere's still room to explore, but the 1E run of it was so legitimately strong and comprehensive that piecing together what remains to explore in ways that work together is a little challenging.<br /> <br /> Not saying it's impossible or that there will never be more books, just saying &quot;DAMN Werewolf already shockingly has so much of it's bases covered.&quot; THe Werewolf line is <i>just that good</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T07:09:08-07:00","id":1460030,"title":"","content":"Yeah I feel like Werewolf doesn't really have any directions to go other than some kind of ground-up &quot;break open setting restrictions&quot; redesign. They did a good job with the 1E line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T09:22:46-07:00","id":1460050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460029#post1460029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem, for Werewolf at least, is that that line was actually kind of <i>too</i> well developed over it's run. THere's still room to explore, but the 1E run of it was so legitimately strong and comprehensive that piecing together what remains to explore in ways that work together is a little challenging.<br /> <br /> Not saying it's impossible or that there will never be more books, just saying &quot;DAMN Werewolf already shockingly has so much of it's bases covered.&quot; THe Werewolf line is <i>just that good</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree pretty strongly on this point. Werewolf 2e has tonnes of open design space.<br /> <br /> One area that I would love to see covered is alternate Moon Gifts. The core book says that Werewolves can pick up Moon Gifts other than the ones listed in the core. Unfortunately, none of the books published to date give examples of alternate Moon Gifts. We have just one semi-official example - Chris Allen made a 2-part open development post on the blog about designing Werewolf Gifts for 2e, and in that he included an example alternate Cahalith Moon Gift. However it is difficult to even find that post today since was made almost 6 years ago.<br /> <br /> Wolf Gifts and Shadow Gifts also pose problems. We have a good number of Shadow Gifts if you include those in Shunned By The Moon, but more would always be welcome. The biggest issue here is that 1e Gifts are totally incompatible with the way Gifts work in 2e, so converting that material would be a tonne of work for any home group to take on. Additionally, there are just three published Wolf Gifts and one semi-official one from the same blog post I mentioned above. That's a lot of open design space, and 1e did not have Wolf Gifts, so there is nothing to borrow from there.<br /> <br /> Lodges are another wide open space. The core book doesn't have any, so the only Lodges we got were in The Pack. Unfortunately that book was trying to do a lot of different things, so Lodges got a fairly short treatment. There are five Lodges in The Pack, two of which are not really compatible with player characters (Temple of Apollo serve either an idigam or a void spirit, and Eaters of the Dead have a ban that requires them to break the Oath of the Moon). That leaves just three official Lodges for player characters. Converting 1e Lodges is similarly difficult. The main benefit 1e Lodges gave you was a discount on Experience costs, which is explicitly not a thing they can do in 2e. Instead, each Lodge needs a unique Blessing, Aspiration, Ban, and Sacred Hunt Refinement, none of which they possessed in 1e, so converting them would be a huge amount of work.<br /> <br /> The other area that needs focus (and goes beyond Werewolf) is the Shadow. Spirits have changed enough from 1e that the Hisil, their relationships, and a lot of example Spirits are things that are frequently asked for by new Storytellers. A new Book of Spirits for 2e would be helpful across many game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T10:40:52-07:00","id":1460058,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but isn't it OPP's policy for now to not retread previous ground, even when similarities are not as deep nowadays ?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'd love for them to make new pure Covenant and Clan Books for Requiem -because they could be translated !- but I don't expect it to happen... and the Circle of the Crone would really need it, its Clanbook was the weakest of the lot and the covenant as changed a lot since then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T10:44:32-07:00","id":1460059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460050#post1460050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lodges are another wide open space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which again, that's not really saying much since a lot of the Z-splats from the other gamelines like Bloodlines, Lodges, and Legacies don't have a lot of official 2e write-ups. It's not something exclusive to Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T11:09:04-07:00","id":1460064,"title":"","content":"Two questions I always ask myself when it comes to what I want in books, with Chronicles at least:<br /> <br /> Unless it's necessary, do I want a new book to invalidate the books I already own on the subject?<br /> <br /> Do I want a new book to assume I am some kind of idiot that can't logicially use what I have to work to my advantage?<br /> <br /> Mind you, sometimes the answer to those is &quot;Yes&quot;, because either time and talent hint at a better working of the material or I find a subject the actual application of my mind to a matter can't work out or otherwise meaningfully let go of.<br /> <br /> A lot of the times, though, the answer is no. The fact that the Second Edition has made the years I spent collecting books on the subject not feel like a waste of time and money is something I very much appreciate, and I've never really had problems with adapting material over when and where I need it.<br /> <br /> I'm always down for more material, but I do wonder how closely people look at their desires in light of that context. As for me, I'd rather wait for a take that's really gonna blow my socks off rather than ask for a return to the treadmill. While some retread or some assumption of explanation is inevitable, I'd rather see products that lean hard into answer <i>no</i> for those questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T11:52:46-07:00","id":1460072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460064#post1460064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really had problems with adapting material over when and where I need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this is a great position to find yourself in. I have neither the time nor the talent required to do this, so right now I feel like all the first edition books I own are useful for flavour but not much else.<br /> <br /> And it seems to me that there's a big difference between saying &quot;Werewolf already has all of its bases covered&quot; and saying &quot;since I have no trouble converting old material, there is no need to revisit ground covered in 1e&quot;.<br /> <br /> As to your two questions, I don't think I have ever felt that a new book invalidated books I already own, and suggesting that those who can't make use of existing material are &quot;some kind of idiot&quot; seems rather unkind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460064#post1460064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me, I'd rather wait for a take that's really gonna blow my socks off rather than ask for a return to the treadmill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the choice between the treadmill and the current situation (no books for Werewolf in over 2 years and none on the horizon) I'd happily take the treadmill. I'd also settle quite happily or a book every year, or even every other year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T12:41:52-07:00","id":1460081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460064#post1460064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it's necessary, do I want a new book to invalidate the books I already own on the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, a lot of us that started playing with 2nd edition don't own the 1st edition books and aren't interested in buying content for a game we're not playing, so there's huge black holes in the setting.<br /> <br /> I would love 1st edition rewrites. People that already own the 1e books wouldn't have to buy them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T13:55:36-07:00","id":1460083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460081#post1460081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, a lot of us that started playing with 2nd edition don't own the 1st edition books and aren't interested in buying content for a game we're not playing, so there's huge black holes in the setting.<br /> <br /> I would love 1st edition rewrites. People that already own the 1e books wouldn't have to buy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is problematic, and is the main issue with second edition. long time fans and loyal customers don't want their books to be invalidated. new customers and arguably the future of CoD don't want outdated books.<br /> Onyx Path is rather unlikely to produce books that either group &quot;wouldn't have to buy&quot; or would be specifically undesirable to half of their customer base. <br /> <br /> My two cents is that even if the game systems in those books aren't an exact match to the 2ed edition they are still worth a read for what can be adapted either mechanically or narratively, and that goes for OWod as well. PDF copies of outdated 1e and OWoD books can be found rather cheap, even free.<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't think the setting black hole is as large as you might think it is. The books and mechanics are modular, use what you like ignore what you don't, change anything as you see fit and any holes are yours to fill in. I've always found CoD/NWoD makes a better toolbox than bible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T14:04:21-07:00","id":1460084,"title":"","content":"Considering Onyx Path doesn't seem to be profiting any off of most of the old books, they would benefit from updating as much as possible.<br /> <br /> That said, regarding Werewolf, while first edition was a tight line there was a lot that was left unexplored or unexplained, and certain key elements that have changed drastically due to simple improvements across edition (notably the tribes and their sacred prey, which retools them from being just social groups). One of the big things left unexplored and, unfortunately, likely to be left unexplored is the Spirit world from its perspective as, at least partial, natives. The Book of Spirits comes closest to focusing on the area but it does so from a mortal point of view, to the level that people I've spoken to who know the Shadow solely through it believe the entire plane is a death trap. Also things like Spirit courts are meant to exist across the world but there's very little information about them or how to build them.<br /> <br /> While the forum may be a small percentage of the actual players and customers of the gameline, it shouldn't be hard to see what's missing or needs to be updated just through skimming through it. The same questions pop up in several lines, clarifications that have never been clarified, rules fragments left hanging. In addition, while there are things that are considered a 'given' to long-term fans, these same things can be complete unknowns to people brought in by second edition, and who are hesitant to buy a book from first edition that's going to be mostly useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T16:42:51-07:00","id":1460099,"title":"","content":"Honestly, a big boon with earlier 2e corebooks was mentioning in the Recommended Reading sections older nWoD/CofD 1e books that could still apply to 2e...that they sadly phased out in later releases.<br /> <br /> (although not listing any Geist 1e books for 2e makes sense considering, well, Geist having the biggest overhaul in mechanics and setting that nothing from 1e can really be applied to 2e without a LOT of rewriting)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T20:26:42-07:00","id":1460106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460016#post1460016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you do that when a lot of the projects are Kickstarter funded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of their Kickstarter in recent years already have the manuscript for the project written before the Kickstarter goes live, so obviously it can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T21:28:29-07:00","id":1460109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1460099#post1460099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although not listing any Geist 1e books for 2e makes sense considering, well, Geist having the biggest overhaul in mechanics and setting that nothing from 1e can really be applied to 2e without a LOT of rewriting)</div> </div> </div> </div>Also because, well. There was <i>one</i> Geist 1e book that existed as a Geist book. Book of the Dead was technically a bluebook, and Geist 1e Core referenced Antagonists, Midnight Roads, Second Sight, and Book of Spirits, but all the Geist 1e material written after the corebook was an SAS or part of a bluebook like Mirrors or Dark Eras. The line was (I think maybe explicitly) built to be a skeleton game as far as supplements went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}